  "boundary": "RTX 3090 sm_86 measurements in synthetic compute mode with accumulation chosen for local tractability. Relative ordering is evidence for configuration selection; absolute throughput and the microbatch and checkpointing decisions must be remeasured on GH200. FLA autotune configurations are Hopper-tuned, so kernel rankings may differ there. No grant GPU-hours were consumed and no data or model was admitted.",
  "date": "2026-09-21",
  "engineering_only": true,
  "findings": {
    "compile_requires_checkpointing_off": "With checkpointing on, compile returns 1.008x because FLA's chunk_kda carries torch.compiler.disable and Dynamo cannot tolerate a break inside a checkpointed region. With it off the same compile returns 1.612x.",
    "conv_rewrite": "One padded buffer with narrowed views instead of one allocation per tap: 1.0165x and 1.72 GiB less backward peak, bitwise identical in forward and backward.",
    "cudagraphs_do_not_help": "0.7% slower; cudagraph_trees cannot capture across the eager KDA islands.",
    "determinism_cost": "1.086x at max-autotune; a larger microbatch more than repays it.",
    "flagship_checkpointing_off_does_not_fit_24gib": "Two attempts reached 23.03 and 22.91 GiB before out-of-memory. The failure is in the backward phase, so reducing Muon's transient cannot unlock it. Decision moves to GH200.",
    "in_kernel_gate_is_a_memory_win": "No measurable throughput change, 1.14 GiB less backward peak at microbatch two.",
    "loader_is_not_a_bottleneck": "End-to-end is 0.6% faster than synthetic compute, inside noise. Loader work was dropped, which also avoids regenerating the loader_check scan pairs.",
    "muon_memory_work_is_unnecessary": "Muon's transient binds peak memory only when checkpointing is on. Across every checkpointing-off configuration the backward phase binds instead, so the planned optimizer memory work would buy nothing and was skipped.",
    "workload_is_bandwidth_bound": "The same code reaches 34.6% MFU on a 3090 against 9.8% on an H100, a card with about fourteen times the peak FLOPS. Throughput tracked memory bandwidth, not compute, so these relative gains are a floor for Hopper rather than a ceiling."
  },
